    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "793891f6_e96557a6",
        "filename": "service/wifi-events.rc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-25T03:08:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two different ways that the property is set:\n\n- Via init: |on boot|, |on post-fs-data|, |on mmi|: all of these come after |post-fs|\n- Via compile-time parameters or files:\n  - PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES\n  - ADDITIONAL_DEFAULT_PROPERTIES\n  - system.prop\n\nTesting this out on my angler, the parameters/files also happen after post-fs. Just to be safe, though, I\u0027ve updated the post-fs event to use the \u0027wifi.interface\u0027 property if available.\n\n(The \"if available\" part is slightly risky, in the sense that it\u0027s also not mentioned in the README.md. However, the \"if available\" feature is used by logcatd.rc. So we\u0027re likely to notice if it\u0027s broken.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 58,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 26
      },
